# libgomp keeps its worker threads alive for the life of the process and never
# joins them, so glibc's per-thread TLS block (allocated in pthread_create)
# is still referenced only from the thread's own stack when R exits. Valgrind
# reports each one as "possibly lost": 368 bytes per worker, one per core
# beyond the first. Not a zurand leak and not fixable from here.
#
# Needed since r-actions turned on --leak-check=full by default, which counts
# possibly-lost blocks in ERROR SUMMARY.
{
   libgomp-thread-pool-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:calloc
   ...
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   ...
   fun:GOMP_parallel
}
